### Demo script for the walkthrough (VS Code REST Client, Rider or Visual Studio).
### Start both services first (see README). Run the requests top to bottom.

@integration = http://localhost:5100
@employee360 = http://localhost:5200

### 1. Happy path: publish an EmployeeUpdated event
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/01-employee-updated.json

### 1a. What happened to it
GET {{integration}}/events/EVT-10452-001

### 1b. Downstream view: updateCount = 1
GET {{employee360}}/api/employees/EMP10452

### 2. Same event delivered again -> Duplicate, nothing sent downstream
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/01-employee-updated.json

### 2a. duplicateDeliveries = 1, and downstream updateCount is still 1
GET {{integration}}/events/EVT-10452-001

###
GET {{employee360}}/api/employees/EMP10452

### 3. "CPT" is normalised to "Cape Town" (and department changes)
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/02-location-alias-cpt.json

### 4. An older event arrives late -> SkippedStale, newer data is not overwritten
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/03-out-of-order-older.json

###
GET {{integration}}/employees/EMP10452

### 5. Bad events are isolated in the dead-letter store
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/04-missing-employee-id.json

###
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/05-malformed.json

###
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/06-unmapped-location.json

### Same eventId as #1 but different content
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/07-conflicting-duplicate.json

###
GET {{integration}}/dead-letters

### 6. Downstream returns 503 twice, then recovers: retried inside one delivery (watch the logs)
POST {{employee360}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "failNext": 2, "statusCode": 503 }

###
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

< ./events/08-new-employee.json

###
GET {{integration}}/events/EVT-20871-001

### 7. Downstream is slow: our call times out, but Employee 360 still applies the update.
###    The retry carries the same Idempotency-Key, so it is not applied twice.
POST {{employee360}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "failNext": 1, "delayMs": 5000 }

###
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EVT-41120-001",
  "eventType": "EmployeeUpdated",
  "employeeId": "EMP41120",
  "firstName": "Pieter",
  "lastName": "van Wyk",
  "department": "Learning",
  "location": "PTA",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-10-04T12:00:00Z"
}

### updateCount = 1
GET {{employee360}}/api/employees/EMP41120

### 8. Downstream outage: retries exhausted across 3 deliveries -> dead-lettered
POST {{employee360}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "failNext": 100, "statusCode": 500 }

###
POST {{integration}}/simulate/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EVT-55501-001",
  "eventType": "EmployeeUpdated",
  "employeeId": "EMP55501",
  "firstName": "Lerato",
  "lastName": "Nkosi",
  "department": "Operations",
  "location": "Durban",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-10-06T08:00:00Z"
}

### After ~40s (3 deliveries x 4 attempts with backoff): status DeadLettered, reason MaxDeliveryCountExceeded
GET {{integration}}/events/EVT-55501-001

### 8a. Outage over: clear the fault and replay the dead letter (use the id from the response above)
DELETE {{employee360}}/chaos

###
POST {{integration}}/dead-letters/5/replay

###
GET {{integration}}/events/EVT-55501-001

### 9. Overall status
GET {{integration}}/status

###
GET {{integration}}/health
